/**
 * Moves the site's shipped content into the CMS — every photograph, and every
 * line of copy that has a field.
 *
 *   npm run seed
 *
 * Afterwards /admin is the site. lib/content.ts and lib/pages stay in the
 * repository as the FALLBACK — what the pages render on a fresh database, or
 * on any request where the database cannot be read (lib/cms/read.ts) — and
 * nothing else. Editing them no longer changes a page that has been seeded.
 *
 * WHAT IT WRITES
 *   media       every photograph the pages ship with, uploaded once
 *   home        the landing page, section by section
 *   pages       all fifteen standing-page globals
 *   projects    one document per address in the shipped rail
 *   posts       the shipped articles, published
 *
 * The photograph mapping is not written out here — it is read off the shipped
 * content. Wherever lib/content.ts or lib/pages uses a file, the field that
 * overrides that spot is filled with the upload of the same file.
 *
 * SAFE TO RE-RUN, AND IT NEVER OVERWRITES AN EDITOR. An upload is found again
 * by its filename rather than sent twice; a project or article that exists is
 * matched by its slug; and a field that already holds something is left alone.
 * "Holds something" is judged deeply — a group whose every input is still
 * blank counts as empty and is filled, a group with one line typed into it is
 * left exactly as it is. So this is also the way to top up a global after new
 * fields are added to it, which is what it was run for when the spread, the
 * practice, the ventures, Vihaa and the responsibility ledger got their copy
 * fields.
 *
 * NORMALISED ON THE WAY IN. EXIF rotation is applied (team/ram.JPG is stored
 * on its side), the long edge is capped at 2560px, opaque images are encoded as
 * JPEG and cut-outs keep their transparency as PNG. Cloudinary then serves each
 * browser its own format and quality.
 *
 * PLACEHOLDER ART IS NOT UPLOADED where a field is optional: an empty field in
 * /admin is the signal that a real photograph is still owed. An article cannot
 * be saved without a photograph, so an article whose shipped card is a
 * placeholder gets one named `placeholder-…`, easy to find and replace.
 *
 * Runs outside Next, like generate:types (see that script for why it is not
 * the Payload CLI). Revalidation is skipped on every write, so restart
 * `next dev` — or wait out the 60-second timer — to see the result.
 */

